      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Formoterol is a new beta 2 agonist with a duration of 8-12 hours. Albuterol is a beta 2-agonist with rapid onset of action and a duration of approximately 6 hours."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The aim of the present study was to compare the onset of action between formoterol and albuterol, both administered through a Turbohaler."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHOD",
          "content": "In a double-blind, parallel-group study design 36 patients were randomly allocated to receive either formoterol 12 microg or salbutamol 200 microg. The two drugs were administered through a Turbohaler system. Response (% forced expiratory volume in one second [FEV1]) was evaluated 3, 30 and 60 minutes after drug administration."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The %FEV1 values at 3, 30 and 60 minutes were similar in both groups: 82 15.0 for formoterol and 82 14.4 for albuterol at 60 minutes (p > 0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Formoterol 12 microg has a similar onset of action and potency to albuterol 200 microg when administered via a Turbuhaler in children with a mild acute asthma crisis."
        }
      ]},
